/-!
# The proof of `prop:torsion-defect-ring`, sentence by sentence

`non_mf_groups_exist.tex`, Proposition `prop:torsion-defect-ring` (tex lines
1072--1120).  One closed `manuscriptSentence_*` theorem per printed sentence of the
proof, stated at the printed generality and proved along the printed route, citing
the declarations of the modules

* `TorsionComplementaryIdempotentsMatrixUnits` (`f_{ij}`),
* `TorsionComplementaryIdempotentsWeyl` (`w_{ij}`, `r`),
* `TorsionComplementaryIdempotentsDiagonal` (`D(a)`),
* `TorsionComplementaryIdempotentsCell` (`v`, `c`, `y`, `z`, `ℓ`),
* `TorsionComplementaryIdempotentsCentral` (`d`, `[y,d]`, the order of `z`),
* `TorsionComplementaryIdempotentsDefect` (`B`, the criterion applied to `B`),
* `TorsionComplementaryIdempotentsSignedPermutations` (the Steinberg relations and
  signed permutations),
* `TorsionComplementaryIdempotents` (the printed proposition).

Coordinates are 0-indexed as everywhere in `OneSidedCompressor`: the printed
coordinates `1,2,3` are `coreIdx 0, coreIdx 1, coreIdx 2`, the printed fourth is
`lastIdx`.  The printed `S` is `Subring.closure {s, t}` and the printed pair inside
it is `pairSubringInverse s t hts`; the printed passage from `EL₄(S)` to `EL_n(R)`
is `pairToRank`, the block embedding followed by the coefficient inclusion.
-/

